    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0151" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/12–1351: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States
                        Representative at the United Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Austin</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d83-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-14T20:26:00-05:00">December 14,
                            1951—8:26 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Gadel 471. Re Delga 659 Dec 13 Dept suggests light possibility Iraq voting for
                    Byelorussia, USDel might if it thinks useful approach <pb facs="0152" n="130"
                        xml:id="pg130"/> Jamali<anchor n="2" xml:id="d83-f2"/> along fol lines: US
                    keenly aware deep interest Iraq in this issue and strongly hopes Jamali in
                    position urge his Govt’s unqualified support for Grk candidacy. Del shld play on
                    theme that US recognizes importance Iraqi Govt attaches Jamali’s
                        recommendations;<anchor n="3" xml:id="d83-f3"/> US therefore approaching him
                    Paris in hope he will recommend to his Govt that it support Greece. Del cld also
                    refer instances his valuable support in past which we greatly appreciate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d83-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d83-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated for information to Baghdad as 321.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f2" n="2" xml:id="d83-f2-content">
                <p>Mohamed Padhil Al-Jamali, Chairman of the Delegation of Iraq to the General
                    Assembly.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d83-f3" n="3" xml:id="d83-f3-content">
                <p>Dr. Jamali was also President of the Iraqi Chamber of Deputies.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
